# File: compiler/patches/agda-language-server-agda-2.9.0.patch
#
# What: support for Agda 2.9.0 in the Agda Language Server, as a flag,
# Agda-2-9-0, beside upstream's Agda-2-8-0, and a branch under
# MIN_VERSION_Agda(2,9,0) wherever Agda 2.9.0's API differs from 2.8.0's;
# 2.8.0's code is kept, so the server still builds against 2.8.0.
#
# Why: no release of the server supports Agda 2.9.0 (issue 58).  At the
# Agda commit compiler/build-agda-2.9.0.sh pins, the API changes the
# server meets are these: ranges store packed intervals (PackIWF); Cohesion
# gains Sharp; ProblemId wraps a Word64; the concrete syntax changes
# IdiomBrackets, DoBlock, Annotation (a rewrite annotation), FunClause (a
# modality), DoOpen, DotP, KnownOpApp, Import, and adds Highlighted and
# EtaEqualityPragma, each rendered here as Agda's own pretty-printer does;
# Dummy terms carry a DummyTermKind; Lisp moved to
# Agda.Interaction.Emacs.Lisp; running info is a document tree, sent as its
# text without annotations, as Agda's JSON frontend sends it; and
# parseFile takes a flag for literate Markdown (False, Agda's default).
# versionString gains a 2.9.0 branch ("Agda v2.9.0 Language Server v8").
# The reactor module used Agda.Setup's setup without importing it, at v8
# and for every Agda from 2.8.0 on; the import is added.
#
# Against: agda/agda-language-server 0f77a209243185cb8e36a11bfc7b6ab47f5125b4
# (tag v8), with Agda da66a8c75f11d10699a6b38b261efdf244b66f2a.  Apply with
# `git apply` in the server's checkout, then run hpack.
#
